### 1. The Protocol Buffer Definition (`playbook.proto`)

First, we define the message types. We need a way to stream lines of text.

```protobuf
syntax = "proto3";

package playbook;

option go_package = "playbook";

// Represents a single line of output from Ansible
message OutputLine {
  string content = 1;
  string timestamp = 2;
}

// Request to start a playbook
message PlaybookRequest {
  string playbook_path = 1;
  string inventory = 2;
  map<string, string> extra_vars = 3;
}

// Response stream
message PlaybookResponse {
  oneof result {
    OutputLine output = 1;
    string error = 2;
    bool finished = 3;
  }
}

// Service definition
service PlaybookService {
  // Unary call to start the stream
  rpc RunPlaybook(PlaybookRequest) returns (stream PlaybookResponse);
}
```

